.TH TCODE 1 "2026-11-07" "T Code 2.1.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tcode \- lightweight text editor written in Lua
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tcode
.RI [ file... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
T Code is a lightweight text editor written mostly in Lua, on top of a
minimalistic C core using the SDL3 graphics library.
.PP
Run with no arguments to open the welcome screen. Pass one or more files
or directories to open them as a project.
.SH PORTABLE MODE
Create a folder named \fBuser\fR next to the \fBtcode\fR binary.
T Code will load and store configuration and plugins in that folder.
Carry the whole directory on a USB drive and your setup travels with you.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LITE_USERDIR
Override the user configuration directory.
.TP
.B LITE_PREFIX
Override the install prefix (expects \fBshare/tcode\fR under it).
.TP
.B LITE_SCALE
UI scale factor (default 1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tcode/
User configuration and plugins (or \fBuser/\fR in portable mode).
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/tcode/ (or $prefix/share/tcode/)
Installed Lua runtime and data.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on fatal error (see error.txt in the user dir).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lua(1)
